{"id": "215a6725-4317-4de9-a7e1-512645bc7906", "timestamp": "2026-06-02T11:14:27.779813", "source": "environment", "tool_name": "terminal", "tool_call_id": "410828cd-e249-45e0-bc7e-2ad3a0e1086a", "observation": {"content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "1\t%{\n     2\t%}\n     3\n     4\t%token <int> INT\n     5\t%token PLUS\n     6\t%token MINUS\n     7\t%token STAR\n     8\t%token SLASH\n     9\t%token LPAREN\n    10\t%token RPAREN\n    11\t%token EOF\n    12\n    13\t%left PLUS MINUS\n    14\t%left STAR SLASH\n    15\t%left LPAREN RPAREN\n    16\n    17\t%start start\n    18\t%type <int> start\n    19\n    20\t%%\n    21\n    22\tstart:\n    23\t  | expr EOF { $1 }\n    24\n    25\texpr:\n    26\t  | a = expr PLUS b = expr { a + b }\n    27\t  | a = expr MINUS b = expr { a - b }\n    28\t  | a = expr STAR b = expr { a * b }\n    29\t  | a = expr SLASH b = expr { a / b }\n    30\t  | INT { $1 }\n    31\t  | LPAREN expr RPAREN { $2 }"}], "is_error": false, "command": "cat -n Parser.fsy", "exit_code": 0, "timeout": false, "metadata": {"exit_code": 0, "pid": -1, "username": "ohama", "hostname": "ohama", "working_dir": "/Users/ohama/projs/OpenHandsTests/oh-workdir-planning/arm-a/fsharp-r1/calc", "py_interpreter_path": "", "prefix": "", "suffix": "\n[The command completed with exit code 0.]"}, "full_output_save_dir": "/Users/ohama/.openhands/conversations/a5fa3ea00138492cbc409945669ab61a/observations", "kind": "TerminalObservation"}, "action_id": "82d3d828-6e02-4734-8c45-0e53484e4901", "kind": "ObservationEvent"}
{"id": "d980af0f-f582-4481-9ace-b7a54a3c99cf", "timestamp": "2026-06-02T11:14:32.138680", "source": "agent", "thought": [], "reasoning_content": null, "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null, "action": {"thought": "The error is on line 26, column 6: `a = expr PLUS b = expr`. The `=` character is unexpected.\n\nThis is because FsYacc doesn't support the `name =` binding syntax in the way I'm using it. In FsYacc, the binding syntax is different. Let me check the correct syntax.\n\nIn FsYacc, the binding syntax uses `name =` but it's for named rules, not for binding in semantic actions. For binding in semantic actions, you use `$1`, `$2`, etc.\n\nLet me rewrite the parser to use positional references:\n\n```\nexpr:\n  | expr PLUS expr { $1 + $3 }\n  | expr MINUS expr { $1 - $3 }\n  | expr STAR expr { $1 * $3 }\n  | expr SLASH expr { $1 / $3 }\n  | INT { $1 }\n  | LPAREN expr RPAREN { $2 }\n```\n\nThis is the standard FsYacc syntax.\n", "kind": "ThinkAction"}, "tool_name": "think", "tool_call_id": "092fdd6c-9724-44cb-a17e-969da5dd6854", "tool_call": {"id": "092fdd6c-9724-44cb-a17e-969da5dd6854", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "think", "arguments": "{\"thought\": \"The error is on line 26, column 6: `a = expr PLUS b = expr`. The `=` character is unexpected.\\n\\nThis is because FsYacc doesn't support the `name =` binding syntax in the way I'm using it. In FsYacc, the binding syntax is different. Let me check the correct syntax.\\n\\nIn FsYacc, the binding syntax uses `name =` but it's for named rules, not for binding in semantic actions. For binding in semantic actions, you use `$1`, `$2`, etc.\\n\\nLet me rewrite the parser to use positional references:\\n\\n```\\nexpr:\\n  | expr PLUS expr { $1 + $3 }\\n  | expr MINUS expr { $1 - $3 }\\n  | expr STAR expr { $1 * $3 }\\n  | expr SLASH expr { $1 / $3 }\\n  | INT { $1 }\\n  | LPAREN expr RPAREN { $2 }\\n```\\n\\nThis is the standard FsYacc syntax.\\n\"}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-5f76a5d3-4666-4de9-b366-b4e1ac4e5cb5", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "critic_result": null, "summary": "think: {\"thought\": \"The error is on line 26, column 6: `a = expr PLUS b = expr`. The `=` character is unexpected.\\n\\nThis is because FsYacc doesn't support the `name =` binding syntax in the way I'm using it. In FsYacc, the binding syntax is different. Let me check the correct syntax.\\n\\nIn FsYacc, the binding syntax uses `name =` but it's for named rules, not for binding in semantic actions. For binding in semantic actions, you use `$1`, `$2`, etc.\\n\\nLet me rewrite the parser to use positional references:\\n\\n```\\nexpr:\\n  | expr PLUS expr { $1 + $3 }\\n  | expr MINUS expr { $1 - $3 }\\n  | expr STAR expr { $1 * $3 }\\n  | expr SLASH expr { $1 / $3 }\\n  | INT { $1 }\\n  | LPAREN expr RPAREN { $2 }\\n```\\n\\nThis is the standard FsYacc syntax.\\n\"}", "kind": "ActionEvent"}
